# TypeScript and CCC

Add `"use client"` only on files that touch CCC, wallet state, or browser APIs. Keep server components as the default.

Split by domain instead of growing one page:

- UI in `components/identity`, `components/dao`, `components/membership`, `components/governance`
- Transaction builders in `lib/ckb/`
- One component or builder per file

When TypeScript mirrors a Rust script, comment capacity, `cellDeps`, and the witness slot next to the builder so the two sides stay aligned.

```tsx
// WitnessArgs.input_type matches the script's input_type slot.
// cellDeps must include the community type script deployed on this network.
const witness = buildMembershipWitness(card)
```

Do not construct transactions inside presentational components.
